WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.140
Open the Credentials page from your private DSH workspace. Confirm

2
00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:08.680
your current account password, then choose an approved connection profile.

3
00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:14.120
Enter an alias, workspace name, permitted actions and expiry. Enter

4
00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:17.680
the provider token only in the dedicated secret field, never

5
00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:21.460
in chat. The browser encrypts that value for the selected

6
00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:25.980
credential broker before submitting it. The broker checks your account,

7
00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:29.960
environment and scope, then stores the value in OpenBao. The

8
00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:33.420
harness receives an alias and permitted results, not the stored

9
00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:38.320
token. No Internet connections use the internal broker. Internet connections

10
00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:42.200
use a separate broker with different network rules. Switching environments

11
00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:45.980
does not transfer connections. A workspace name is a policy

12
00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:49.580
label inside your private runtime, not a separate execution boundary

13
00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:51.240
between your own projects.

14
00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:54.780
Use the connection adapter to list your aliases and request

15
00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:59.780
an approved operation. Read operations stay within the selected resources.

16
00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:02.660
A write request waits for your confirmation in the Credentials

17
00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:07.560
page. Review its parameters before approving it once. Changed requests

18
00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:10.940
and replayed approvals are denied. If a write has an

19
00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:15.700
uncertain outcome, check the provider before requesting another write. Central

20
00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:20.400
activity records exclude secret values. You can replace, disable or

21
00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:24.220
delete your stored connection. Deleting it stops broker access, but

22
00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:28.820
provider revocation remains a separate action. Existing login passwords and

23
00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:33.300
Kerberos authentication are unchanged. This release supports configured API token

24
00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:37.240
and personal access token connectors; it does not provide OAuth

25
00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:42.060
consent or Kerberos ticket acquisition. Operators retain encrypted backups and

26
00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:45.220
use a separate protected recovery process when the vault restarts

27
00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:46.000
sealed.
